+### R31 · The memory plane's tiering asymmetry — `adapt_cleanroom`
+
+**Evidence trail (one-grep verifiable, main b4792b8):**
+
+| Surface | Anchor | What exists today | What is missing |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Tower | live `tools/list` 2026-10-28 | 21 `memory_*` tools: `memory_search_semantic`, `memory_ingest_document_rag`, `memory_get_similar_tasks`, `memory_build_context`, `memory_search_learned_facts`, knowledge-graph CRUD | — (rich tier already landed) |
+| Agent CLI | `scripts/agents/agent_solution_memory.py:60-66` | `search_local_lessons`: `re.split(r"[\s,:;\-_]+", query)`, terms `len>2`, substring over `LESSONS_LEARNED.md` | semantic/similar-task recall; cannot reach the tower tier from its own search path |
+| Gateway | `gateway/service/memory_store.py:102-124` | `user_memories(id, user_id, memory_key, memory_value, confidence, source_conv_id, updated_at)` | entity resolution, consolidation/decay, supersede semantics for reused keys, provenance chain |
+
+**External pattern references (live-probed 2026-10-28, pattern extraction ONLY):**
