+- **Pros:** the expensive tier (semantic + RAG + episodic) is ALREADY landed at the tower — wiring beats rebuilding; zero new dependencies (tower tools are reachable through the existing zero-credential MCP session pattern); the Search-Before-Solving workflow (`agent_solution_memory.py` step 1) gets materially smarter without any schema change; graceful-degradation contract keeps the offline path honest.
+- **Cons:** adds a runtime dependency on tower availability for the richer tier (mitigated by the local-first, fallback-only design); tier labels add output surface that tests must pin.
+- **Risks:** silently treating tower results as ground truth (mitigated: every hit labeled with its tier); drift if tower tools rename (mitigated: fail-closed fallback keeps local tier authoritative).
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no mem0/graphiti vendoring (Gold Pearl doctrine: 20–100-line native slices only); no vector DB or embedding-service dependency in slice 1 (tower owns the semantic tier — duplicating it repo-side is anti-SSOT); no weakening of the gateway 3-tier store contract.
