+### R32 · Search supply: one SSOT exists, a second brittle path scrapes around it — `adapt_cleanroom`
+
+**Live probe table (all 2026-10-28, scout UA, unauthenticated):**
+
+| Probe | Result | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET duckduckgo.com/html/?q=…` | **HTTP 202**, 14 KB HTML interstitial (anti-bot anomaly class), zero parseable results | the exact endpoint `deep_research.py` scrapes already serves challenge pages to non-browser clients |
+| same URL, browser UA | **connection reset** | fingerprint blocking — scrape viability is luck, not contract |
+| `GET lite.duckduckgo.com/lite/?q=…` | HTTP 200 HTML | works today; same fragility class, no SLA |
+| `GET api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search?q=…` | **HTTP 422** validating `x-subscription-token` | live, key-gated, protocol-speaking |
+| `POST api.tavily.com/search {}` | **HTTP 401** `missing or invalid API key` | live, key-gated, protocol-speaking |
+| `POST api.exa.ai/search {}` | HTTP 404 | inconclusive — **EXCLUDED** (zero-hype) |
+| `GET searx.be/search?format=json` / `searx.tiekoetter.com` | 200-but-HTML (JSON disabled) / **429** | public SearXNG unusable programmatically — self-host lane only, not smallest slice |
+
+**Internal drift proof:** `gateway/routes/deep_research.py:220` (byte-identical mirror
+`core/api/routes/deep_research.py:220`, parity-verified per the #1720 sentinel) builds the DDG html URL and
+feeds `CrawlerService.execute_crawl` — while `core/search.py:20-55` already implements the resilient path
+(`core/pyproject.toml:24` pins `ddgs = "^9.16.0"`, ddgs-first import, exception-safe `web_search()`).
+`rg -i "tavily|brave|serpapi|exa" gateway/` → zero presence. Two search implementations, one implicit SSOT.
+
+- **Pros:** consolidation is a swap, not a build — the SSOT client is landed and pinned; the mirror pair is
+  sentinel-guarded so atomicity is mechanically enforced; env-keyed fallback mirrors the provider_registry's
+  own doctrine ("keys come from environment!", fail-closed); key-less runs keep the zero-cost contract
+  (`core/pyproject.toml` documents শূন্য-খরচ / no-API-key).
+- **Cons:** Brave/Tavily are paid-after-free-tier — must stay strictly optional and never default-on; one
+  more env surface to document.
+- **Risks:** ddgs itself is scrape-derived and can degrade (that is exactly why the fallback lane is keyed
+  providers, and why the degradation must stay honest-warn, never crash); mirror drift if the two files are
+  edited separately (mitigated: single-commit mirror-atomic requirement + sentinel).
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no search-provider SDK dependency (plain JSON calls); no hard failure when keys are
+  absent; no single-sided mirror edits (parity guard fails it — by design); no retry/proxy-rotation arms race
+  against an anti-bot wall — Superior Replacement replaces the approach, it does not fight the wall.
+- **Adoption path → Issue [#1751](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1751)**
+  (Parent Anchor Hub #750 — Unified Provider Gateway): consolidate both mirror files onto
+  `core.search.web_search`, map to the existing `{title, url, snippet, source:"scout"}` shape, optional
+  `SUPREME_SEARCH_BRAVE_KEY` / `SUPREME_SEARCH_TAVILY_KEY` fail-closed templates.
